sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/empty-shell-morphospace> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Why is shell morphospace empty where it is?" ;
    dct:description "In Raup's parameter space of coiled shells (whorl expansion W, distance from axis D, translation T), is the unoccupied region explained by developmental constraint, functional selection (strength, hydrodynamics, stability) or phylogenetic inertia, and can these be told apart quantitatively?" ;

    skos:historyNote "Known state: Raup (1966) showed realized shells occupy a small, structured part of the theoretical space. Fifty years of theoretical morphology (reviewed by Gerber 2017) have proposed functional and constructional explanations, but no accepted test discriminates them, partly because digitized shell parameter data were sparse. Thompson's shell-form claims (ch11) assume the logarithmic-spiral generative model." ;
    dct:subject "both" ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "open-problem/tier-B" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Resolved when: A pre-registered test on digitized museum shell datasets (parameters measured by the morpholib MorphoEval pipeline), fitting explicit occupancy models: a developmental-constraint model (parameter correlations imposed by the generating curve), a functional model (strength and stability thresholds) and a phylogenetic model, compared by predictive likelihood on held-out taxa." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Resolved when: An empty-region map with the winning model's predicted boundaries." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Refuted if: If no model beats a phylogenetic random walk on held-out taxa, the question stays open with present data." ;
    skos:note "Data access: Digitized shell collections (MorphoSource, iDigBio, open), Raup parameters re-measured; taxon resolution via test-data/organisms." ;
    skos:note "Requires: theoretical-morphology" ;
    skos:note "Requires: morpholib" ;
    skos:note "Requires: 3d-shape-analysis" ;
    skos:note "Requires: data-test" ;
    skos:note "Scale: organism" ;
    skos:note "Scale: evolutionary" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-09> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-11> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-05> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-15> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.jstor.org/stable/1301405> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1111/brv.12276> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/e77f4bcffb077981b60f1e3aea24b72c7a36b2fc/problems/problems.json> .

  <https://www.jstor.org/stable/1301405> dct:bibliographicCitation "Raup 1966, Geometric analysis of shell coiling: general problems" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1111/brv.12276> dct:title "The geometry of morphospaces: lessons from the classic\n                    <scp>R</scp>\n                    aup shell coiling model" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Gerber 2017, The geometry of morphospaces: lessons from the classic Raup shell coiling model" .
}

